# The left-to-right pinning around a hoisted error-carrying hole holds in
# every position that hoists: an attribute value, a component input, a class
# part and guard, an if condition (after its init statement), a switch tag, a
# value-form arm, a native and a component conditional-attribute branch (inside
# the branch / the AttrsCond thunk), a spread, an attrs-literal pair, a literal
# nested in another literal's hole, a js` literal, a literal whose own earlier
# hole is pinned after the field's operands, two hoisting literals with a call
# between them, an element literal inside a pinned call, a conditional
# attribute's condition and switch tag, a value-form if condition and switch
# tag, an else-if header with an init statement, a marker name, and <script>
# and <style> holes, a component's conditional-attribute condition, and
# (across fields, already ordered) an earlier attribute's call, and an
# interpolation inside an element literal in top-level Go, and a piped
# interpolation. Each line
# records the order its calls ran in; every line reads g (or 1/mid) before 2.
